{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1755319,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue_un","paid":0,"title":"TinkerCase 4.0","festival_id":514223,"organization_id":306,"web_url":"ieeeday.ieeedtu.in\/","start_date":"2026-09-13T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-16T15:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/tinkercase-40-ieee-day-2026-dtu-new-delhi-1755319","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>TinkerCase 4.0:<\/strong>&nbsp;<strong>IEEE DTU's Hardware Showcase &amp; Core Electronics Event<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Guidelines:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Team size: 1-4 members<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Each team must bring their own laptops<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Hardware models must be fully assembled before the competition;&nbsp; no extra assembly time will be given<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Every participant must carry valid ID proof<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Every team should bring their own extension cords if they feel a need to use it.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The decisions of the organizers shall be final<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Event Format:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Tracks -<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Sustainability &amp; Green Electronics<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Healthcare<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Consumer Electronics<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Robotics<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Safety &amp; Security<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Digital Electronics\/VLSI<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Open Innovation<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 1 &ndash; Idea Submission (Online, via Unstop)<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Participants will submit their project idea through Unstop as a PowerPoint presentation (maximum of&nbsp; 4 slides), covering:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Introduction: Project title, team name, and a brief summary<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Technical Explanation: Key technologies and methodology used<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Real-Life Application: Practical use, impact, and scalability<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Conclusion (Optional): Summary and next steps<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Selected teams will be shortlisted to report to DTU for an offline hardware showcase with their projects.<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Submission Deadline: TBD<\/span><\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 2 &ndash; Hardware Showcase (On-Campus)<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Participants must bring their hardware models fully assembled; no additional assembly time will be provided at the venue.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Each team will pitch their idea to the judges alongside a live demonstration of their hardware project.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Time: 5 minutes per team for presentation in front of the judges.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Date: 16th October<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Venue: DTU Main Campus<\/span><\/p>\n<p><strong>Complementary Quiz (Open Event)<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Right after the inauguration, kick back and test your knowledge!<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;Time: 11:00 AM &ndash; 1:00 PM [Right after inauguration]<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Open to all Tinkercase participants and any other attendees who wish to join<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Prizes: IEEE Goodies<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a title=\"WhatsApp Link\" href=\"https:\/\/chat.whatsapp.com\/JrynEpIoBRx7P2cgrqHEKv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https:\/\/chat.whatsapp.com\/JrynEpIoBRx7P2cgrqHEKv<\/a><br \/>Website: <a href=\"https:\/\/ieeeday.ieeedtu.in\/\">Visit the IEEE DAY website here<\/a><br \/><\/span><\/p>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":8454706,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-09-13T21:18:22+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-07T00:36:19+05:30","communication_sent":1,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"innovation_challenge","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"yJVqa6D","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":1,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked